.TH RUNNER 1 "2026-07-31" "irix-actions-runner 0.4.0-rc2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runner \- GitHub Actions self-hosted runner for SGI IRIX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runner configure
.B \-\-url
.I URL
.B \-\-token
.I TOKEN
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner run
.RI [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-verbose | \-\-trace ]
.br
.B runner serve
.RI [ \-\-count
.I N
.B \-\-name\-prefix
.IR P ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner execjob
.B \-\-message
.I FILE
.B \-\-name
.I NAME
.B \-\-work
.I DIR
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner remove
.B \-\-token
.I TOKEN
.RI [ \-\-count
.I N
.B \-\-name\-prefix
.IR P ]
.br
.B runner status
.RI [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B runner selftest
.RI [ host ]
.br
.B runner version
.br
.B runner help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native GitHub Actions runner for IRIX 6.5.22 and later. Implements the runner
protocol in C99.
.PP
.B run
listens for jobs and executes them in the current process.
.B serve
runs a Linux-hosted pool and starts one worker container per job.
.B execjob
runs one job message without local runner configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS configure
Registers with GitHub and writes runner state. Generates a 2048-bit RSA key;
the registration token is not used after registration.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Repository or organisation URL:
.I https://github.com/ORG
or
.IR https://github.com/ORG/REPO .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Registration token from the repository or organisation Actions settings or
registration-token API. Required. Tokens expire after one hour.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Runner name. Defaults to the hostname, or
.I irix\-runner
if
.BR gethostname (3)
fails. Excluded by
.BR \-\-count .
.TP
.BI \-\-runnergroup " NAME"
Runner group. Default:
.IR Default .
The group must have access to the target repository. A runner in an
inaccessible group appears Online but receives no jobs.
.TP
.BI \-\-labels " A,B,C"
Extra labels beyond
.IR irix ,
.I mips
and
.IR mips\-n32 .
Maximum 32 labels in total.
.TP
.BI \-\-work " DIR"
Work directory. Default:
.IR _work .
Excluded by
.BR \-\-count .
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Replace an existing runner with the same name. Without this flag, an existing
.I .runner
file is refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Register 1 to 64 identities as
.IR P\-0 " through " P\-(N\-1) .
Each identity gets its own directory, runner name and work directory, plus the
.I emulated
label. Requires
.BR \-\-name\-prefix ;
excludes
.BR \-\-name " and " \-\-work .
.TP
.BI \-\-name\-prefix " P"
Directory and runner-name prefix for
.BR \-\-count .
Maximum 112 bytes.
.SS run
Listens for jobs and executes them in the current process. The configured
runner appears Online while this command is running. Supported on IRIX and
Linux.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Runner directory. Default: current directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-\-trace
Enable protocol logging. Trace is more verbose.
.SS serve
Linux only. Runs one listener per identity and one worker container per job.
Returns 2 on IRIX.
.PP
All identity directories are validated before listeners start. SIGINT and
SIGTERM are forwarded to every listener. Startup removes worker containers
left by a previous
.B serve
process.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Serve 1 to 64 identities. Requires
.BR \-\-name\-prefix .
.TP
.BI \-\-name\-prefix " P"
Use identity directories
.IR P\-0 ,
.IR P\-1 ,
and so on.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " NAME"
Worker image. Default:
.IR ghcr.io/sgidevnet/irix\-worker:latest .
Missing images are pulled once before the create is retried.
.TP
.BI \-\-job\-timeout " SECS"
Container wall-clock limit, 1 to 86400 seconds. Default: 14400. Starts when the
container starts. On expiry, the host kills the container and reports the job
failed. Not passed into the guest.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-\-trace
Enable protocol logging. Trace is more verbose.
.SS execjob
Runs and reports one job message. The message contains its reporting
credentials; no local registration is required. Used inside worker guests.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " FILE"
Job message file. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Runner name reported to the job. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-work " DIR"
Absolute work directory, under 128 bytes. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-cancel\-file " PATH"
Abort when the existing file's mtime changes. Polled every 5 seconds.
.SS remove
Deregisters the runner and deletes local configuration. Requires a fresh
registration token. Accepts the same
.BR \-\-count " and " \-\-name\-prefix
pair as
.BR configure .
.PP
For a pool, continues after individual failures and returns 1 if any identity
failed.
.SS status
Prints the runner name, URL, group, pool id, agent id, tenant, broker mode, JWT
algorithm and work directory. Returns 1 if no runner is configured.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Runner directory. Default: current directory.
.SS selftest
Checks HTTPS against
.I host
(default
.IR api.github.com ):
status, server header, body size, clock skew, JSON parsing and connection
reuse. On Linux, also checks the Docker socket and prints the daemon version.
.PP
Returns 1 if a check fails. Does not check or pull the worker image.
.SS version
Prints the project version and reported protocol version. Also
.BR \-\-version " and " \-V .
.SS help
Prints the usage summary. Also
.BR \-\-help " and " \-h .
.SH LABELS
Every runner has the custom labels
.IR irix ,
.I mips
and
.IR mips\-n32 ,
plus the system labels
.IR self\-hosted ,
.I Linux
and
.IR X64 .
GitHub has no IRIX or MIPS system labels; use the custom labels in
.IR runs\-on .
.PP
.B configure \-\-count
adds
.IR emulated .
For hardware-only jobs, add a hardware label with
.B \-\-labels
and require it in
.IR runs\-on .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .runner
Runner identity and server URLs. Mode 0644.
.TP
.I .credentials
OAuth client id and token endpoint. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I .rsakey
PKCS#1 PEM private key. Mode 0600. Other modes produce a warning.
.TP
.I cert.pem
Trust roots. Used automatically when located beside the binary.
.PP
.B \-\-count
stores one set of runner files in each identity directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SGUG_RUNNER_OS
OS value sent to GitHub and exported to steps as
.BR RUNNER_OS .
Default:
.IR Linux .
.TP
.B SSL_CERT_FILE
Trust-root file. If unset, the runner uses
.I cert.pem
beside the binary, then
.IR /usr/sgug/etc/pki/tls/cert.pem .
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Docker socket for
.BR serve .
Default:
.IR /var/run/docker.sock .
Only
.I unix://
URLs are accepted.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Parent for mode 0700 job directories created by
.BR serve .
Default:
.IR /tmp .
.TP
.B SGUG_DUMP_MESSAGES
Print every received message body. Messages contain access tokens and workflow
secrets. For protocol debugging only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, unknown command, or
.B serve
on IRIX.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register and run one repository runner:
.PP
.RS
.nf
runner configure \-\-url https://github.com/OWNER/REPO \-\-token TOK
runner run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register and serve four organisation runners:
.PP
.RS
.nf
runner configure \-\-url https://github.com/ORG \-\-token TOK \\
    \-\-count 4 \-\-name\-prefix irix \-\-runnergroup IRIX
runner serve \-\-count 4 \-\-name\-prefix irix
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
An acquired job must be completed. A job lost before completion leaves the
identity Online at
.I currentParallelism 1
but unavailable for further dispatch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR gh (1)
.PP
.I https://github.com/sgidevnet/irix\-actions\-runner
